    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29463" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσπρόσ-οδος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>difficult of access</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.65
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				28.1
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τοῖς ἐναντίοις πόλις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1330b3
				</span></i>
			; <i>hard to assault</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάξις,
				παρεμβολή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.26.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.65.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of men,
				<i>unsocial</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. αὑτὸν παρέχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.130
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Scyth.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				11.6
			</span></i>.</div>
